### FinTech

26. What challenges are unique to banking applications?
->
• Security is paramount—data breaches have severe consequences.
• Regulatory compliance (PCI-DSS, RBI guidelines) complicates development.
• High reliability expectations—downtime affects millions of users.
• Complex transaction logic with multiple states and failure scenarios.
• Performance is critical as banking apps handle high transaction volumes.

...........

27. How do you build secure Android applications?
->
• Use encrypted storage (DataStore, EncryptedSharedPreferences) for sensitive data.
• Never hardcode secrets; use secure backend APIs.
• Implement certificate pinning to prevent MITM attacks.
• Validate all inputs and use HTTPS for network communication.
• Regularly update dependencies and monitor security advisories.

...........

28. Why is reliability important in fintech?
->
• Users trust banking apps with their money and personal data.
• A crash during transaction can cause financial loss or data inconsistency.
• Unreliable apps damage brand reputation and lose customers.
• Regulatory penalties apply if systems fail to meet uptime SLAs.
• Reliability directly correlates with user satisfaction and retention.

...........

29. How would you handle sensitive user data?
->
• Minimize data collection—store only what's necessary.
• Encrypt data at rest and in transit.
• Use secure backend APIs rather than storing credentials on device.
• Implement proper access controls and audit logs.
• Comply with regulations like GDPR and data retention policies.

...........

30. What role does testing play in banking applications?
->
• Testing prevents financial transactions from failing or losing data.
• Comprehensive tests catch edge cases in complex payment workflows.
• Automated tests enable confident deployments and quick rollbacks.
• Regression testing ensures critical paths remain stable after updates.
• Testing in fintech is not optional—it's a compliance and safety requirement.

